00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:33.660
This frustrating scenario is more common than many project managers admit.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:40.000
The issue frequently traces to inconsistent, low-level laboratory contamination controls

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:46.640
when laboratories switch between standard hydrocarbon suites and emerging contaminant methods that

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:55.040
demand far stricter blank performance. Under ISO 17.025 accreditation, laboratories must demonstrate

00:08:55.040 --> 00:09:01.000
