00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:38.580
summary table alone. They also insist on batch specific blank data when samples cross multiple

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:45.240
contaminant classes. The most common mistake is assuming that accreditation for PFAS automatically

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:51.540
means the laboratory applies the same rigorous contamination controls to every sample stream.

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:58.680
The practical fix is straightforward. Specify in the chain of custody and quality assurance plan

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:04.840
that all blanks must be reported at the project's specific reporting limit for both analyte groups

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:11.560
before data validation proceeds. Taking this step early can save weeks of resampling,

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:18.380
